      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 96221,
      "raw_sha256": "32f65c3fd7b7b1bb4d250acfacbcd6a719e46c43f9d23bc4c821fc67f4c55ef7",
      "lf_sha256": "32f65c3fd7b7b1bb4d250acfacbcd6a719e46c43f9d23bc4c821fc67f4c55ef7",
      "source_text": "Our algorithm operates on the augmented distribution underlying the proximal sampler of Lee, Shen, and Tian [ 17 ] . For a scale \\eta\\in(0,1/\\beta] , consider the joint law",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.SS2.p1.1"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E6",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 96222,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 98215,
      "raw_sha256": "1f01e27c8eb38fd05a57d820c65ee6b36832171cce845e8cd1b52f4588526375",
      "lf_sha256": "1f01e27c8eb38fd05a57d820c65ee6b36832171cce845e8cd1b52f4588526375",
      "source_text": "\\pi_{\\eta}(\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\,. (2.6)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.E6"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-96284-98198",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 96284,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 98198,
      "raw_sha256": "e1f1d5707dfa86bc056643b9b125f748e3a32d14ba620e0124c107702527b0ff",
      "lf_sha256": "e1f1d5707dfa86bc056643b9b125f748e3a32d14ba620e0124c107702527b0ff",
      "source_text": "\\pi_{\\eta}(\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\,. (2.6)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-96284-98198"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.SS2.p1.2",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 98216,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 98825,
      "raw_sha256": "924484e75d2b466b5cec5a63a9a814e76aa622d20f2640418354b4f2eb2a5a76",
      "lf_sha256": "924484e75d2b466b5cec5a63a9a814e76aa622d20f2640418354b4f2eb2a5a76",
      "source_text": "The original proximal sampler algorithm performs Gibbs sampling on \\pi_{\\eta} . Namely, under \\pi_{\\eta} one may generate the joint state as",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.SS2.p1.2"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E7",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 98826,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 100299,
      "raw_sha256": "2be554d84baf1f2b796ade05fba49271b5d05e4e8d2d46427d47a6756f85c8f9",
      "lf_sha256": "2be554d84baf1f2b796ade05fba49271b5d05e4e8d2d46427d47a6756f85c8f9",
      "source_text": "X\\sim\\mu\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\ \\text{independently}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY=X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,. (2.7)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.E7"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-98888-100282",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 98888,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 100282,
      "raw_sha256": "84d3ba054a6170f67ea5c7de3c5443c7c5bb05d53cdc5de0e9db4690f7c4c634",
      "lf_sha256": "84d3ba054a6170f67ea5c7de3c5443c7c5bb05d53cdc5de0e9db4690f7c4c634",
      "source_text": "X\\sim\\mu\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\ \\text{independently}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY=X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,. (2.7)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-98888-100282"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.SS2.p1.3",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 100300,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 103210,
      "raw_sha256": "88acd72591b34c91b79748a608c4055defcc626177d46412bb70d6de7b478c32",
      "lf_sha256": "88acd72591b34c91b79748a608c4055defcc626177d46412bb70d6de7b478c32",
      "source_text": "Its X -marginal is \\pi_{\\eta}^{X}=\\mu . Write \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y} for the Y -marginal, so that \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}(\\mathrm{d}y)\\propto e^{-U_{\\eta}(y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y ; by ( 2.7 ), \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y}=\\mu*\\mathcal{N}(0,\\eta I) is a Gaussian smoothing of the target. We use superscripts for marginal and conditional laws; in particular,",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.SS2.p1.3"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E8",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 103211,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 105641,
      "raw_sha256": "f72b9e301f7145614d1dcdad5cba42f06d2b7a1723a29fa65b1f16555b238584",
      "lf_sha256": "f72b9e301f7145614d1dcdad5cba42f06d2b7a1723a29fa65b1f16555b238584",
      "source_text": "\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y\\mid X=x}=\\mathcal{N}(x,\\eta I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,. (2.8)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.E8"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-103273-105624",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 103273,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 105624,
      "raw_sha256": "6ccb54d4fe622363401b987a5f655f9269ce84cd7748a0fc4603863962172b16",
      "lf_sha256": "6ccb54d4fe622363401b987a5f655f9269ce84cd7748a0fc4603863962172b16",
      "source_text": "\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y\\mid X=x}=\\mathcal{N}(x,\\eta I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,. (2.8)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-103273-105624"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.SS2.p1.4",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Proximal/RGO algorithm convention or complexity motivation; not required for Eq2.13/D.6 marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 105642,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 108042,
      "raw_sha256": "849c2a1835e03020a514d031b11576bc09edaa8163dd4a453309899e04de0d04",
      "lf_sha256": "849c2a1835e03020a514d031b11576bc09edaa8163dd4a453309899e04de0d04",
      "source_text": "Gibbs sampling alternates exact draws from the two conditional laws in ( 2.8 ). The scale \\eta controls the strength of the quadratic coupling potential. Decreasing \\eta makes X and Y more tightly coupled and the conditional law of X given Y more localized and better conditioned, which reduces the cost of conditional sampling. The resulting transitions are also more local, however, and generally require more Gibbs sampling iterations. Thus \\eta balances the cost of each iteration against the number of iterations. The convergence and query complexity are studied further in [ 6 , 9 , 15 ] ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.SS2.p2.1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 108088,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 108558,
      "raw_sha256": "9983e3263975bad3391bdcaa65992c69baad4a0547981cacefcac2ac7f30a679",
      "lf_sha256": "9983e3263975bad3391bdcaa65992c69baad4a0547981cacefcac2ac7f30a679",
      "source_text": "The next proposition collects the basic geometric properties of the augmented distribution used throughout the paper: the curvature and concentration of the conditional law, the curvature of the Y -marginal, and a reflection symmetry of the joint law.",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.SS2.p2.1"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.Thmtheorem1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "source-statement",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 108566,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 122098,
      "raw_sha256": "72cd924958c7284c256bb467463abdb3f9590f4f0d31e51d852f49345e0f5aa0",
      "lf_sha256": "72cd924958c7284c256bb467463abdb3f9590f4f0d31e51d852f49345e0f5aa0",
      "source_text": "Proposition 2.1 (Geometry of the joint law) . The joint law ( 2.6 ) has the following properties. (i) For every y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d} , the conditional law \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} has potential (that is, negative log-density up to an additive constant) V_{y}(x)\\coloneqq V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\,. (2.9) This conditional potential satisfies (\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V_{y}(x)\\preceq(\\beta+\\eta^{-1})I\\,, (2.10) so its condition number is at most (1+\\beta\\eta)/(1+\\alpha\\eta)\\leq 2 . Consequently, for every smooth f , \\Var_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(f)\\leq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}\\|\\nabla f\\|^{2}\\,, (2.11) and \\frac{\\eta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\preceq\\mathrm{Cov}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(X)\\preceq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\,. (2.12) (ii) The Y -marginal potential satisfies \\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}U_{\\eta}(y)\\preceq\\frac{\\beta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\,. (2.13) (iii) The state-space reflection \\mathsf{U}:(x,y)\\mapsto(x,2x-y) (2.14) preserves \\pi_{\\eta} and is an involution.",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.Thmtheorem1"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 109025,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 109475,
      "raw_sha256": "6c71b1f543b3beefbefa2de494478798fa3befa2026a96fb323333b917dc55ef",
      "lf_sha256": "6c71b1f543b3beefbefa2de494478798fa3befa2026a96fb323333b917dc55ef",
      "source_text": "The joint law ( 2.6 ) has the following properties.",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.I1.i1.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 109703,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 110676,
      "raw_sha256": "2b217fbe54553452b144f42f34e4107a5fb82a3bcc19f9ac2bd70fe2b10abce4",
      "lf_sha256": "2b217fbe54553452b144f42f34e4107a5fb82a3bcc19f9ac2bd70fe2b10abce4",
      "source_text": "For every y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d} , the conditional law \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} has potential (that is, negative log-density up to an additive constant)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.I1.i1.p1.1"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E9",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 110677,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 111985,
      "raw_sha256": "0eee1430d82a367d693bd62e4adfd8f9d8926c7ad2998204ad7801f47231728f",
      "lf_sha256": "0eee1430d82a367d693bd62e4adfd8f9d8926c7ad2998204ad7801f47231728f",
      "source_text": "V_{y}(x)\\coloneqq V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\,. (2.9)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.E9"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-110739-111968",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 110739,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 111968,
      "raw_sha256": "eafd1e39660e3751b15495fbbdb3e40e4255456c3688b4d61ce03725c41ba731",
      "lf_sha256": "eafd1e39660e3751b15495fbbdb3e40e4255456c3688b4d61ce03725c41ba731",
      "source_text": "V_{y}(x)\\coloneqq V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\,. (2.9)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-110739-111968"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.I1.i1.p1.2",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 111986,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 112129,
      "raw_sha256": "811516f7e4589759f825012147fea25c073a89712ac24dbe79b6208e40c5626f",
      "lf_sha256": "811516f7e4589759f825012147fea25c073a89712ac24dbe79b6208e40c5626f",
      "source_text": "This conditional potential satisfies",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.I1.i1.p1.2"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E10",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 112130,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 113641,
      "raw_sha256": "540ecdc7b0e82cfb6c35e2be696b9237b8211b2a0fa99b4fc7b0efd4fc765347",
      "lf_sha256": "540ecdc7b0e82cfb6c35e2be696b9237b8211b2a0fa99b4fc7b0efd4fc765347",
      "source_text": "(\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V_{y}(x)\\preceq(\\beta+\\eta^{-1})I\\,, (2.10)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.E10"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-112193-113624",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 112193,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 113624,
      "raw_sha256": "ece3aebf554be5166fe019e044e60d34a52345ef86a360651d64d3d8b9161955",
      "lf_sha256": "ece3aebf554be5166fe019e044e60d34a52345ef86a360651d64d3d8b9161955",
      "source_text": "(\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V_{y}(x)\\preceq(\\beta+\\eta^{-1})I\\,, (2.10)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-112193-113624"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.I1.i1.p1.3",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 113642,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 114782,
      "raw_sha256": "4f7ea7776cefbdce38f2cb4bf1d9932bee72fcf8f5f9297a7016c3b7456b8c60",
      "lf_sha256": "4f7ea7776cefbdce38f2cb4bf1d9932bee72fcf8f5f9297a7016c3b7456b8c60",
      "source_text": "so its condition number is at most (1+\\beta\\eta)/(1+\\alpha\\eta)\\leq 2 . Consequently, for every smooth f ,",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.I1.i1.p1.3"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E11",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 114783,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 116492,
      "raw_sha256": "b5c67354e00bad60bacdd95d7c3be5368517a600f52898c56493f12393c160fb",
      "lf_sha256": "b5c67354e00bad60bacdd95d7c3be5368517a600f52898c56493f12393c160fb",
      "source_text": "\\Var_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(f)\\leq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}\\|\\nabla f\\|^{2}\\,, (2.11)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.E11"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-114846-116475",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 114846,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 116475,
      "raw_sha256": "f4628af8c44ca2870bfe721e500c1cd890fdf73a02ad6e35db66d6323c3b3b44",
      "lf_sha256": "f4628af8c44ca2870bfe721e500c1cd890fdf73a02ad6e35db66d6323c3b3b44",
      "source_text": "\\Var_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(f)\\leq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}\\|\\nabla f\\|^{2}\\,, (2.11)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-114846-116475"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.I1.i1.p1.4",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 116493,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 116603,
      "raw_sha256": "c4c7c3bc0b57bc669d75f49a0aaf235b3e871c9057b8f863546b5a5d31d8d37e",
      "lf_sha256": "c4c7c3bc0b57bc669d75f49a0aaf235b3e871c9057b8f863546b5a5d31d8d37e",
      "source_text": "and",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.I1.i1.p1.4"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E12",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 116604,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 118189,
      "raw_sha256": "e71317ceb0d7f8d91796cbad1fee9babcd6d48bdcbb67022c3462d08ab0bc4bc",
      "lf_sha256": "e71317ceb0d7f8d91796cbad1fee9babcd6d48bdcbb67022c3462d08ab0bc4bc",
      "source_text": "\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\preceq\\mathrm{Cov}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(X)\\preceq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\,. (2.12)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.E12"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-116667-118172",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 116667,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 118172,
      "raw_sha256": "6112d2b37d5e1e64a65ea004f5dddb2135170d98f5b8928dcde460aee3eae9a2",
      "lf_sha256": "6112d2b37d5e1e64a65ea004f5dddb2135170d98f5b8928dcde460aee3eae9a2",
      "source_text": "\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\preceq\\mathrm{Cov}_{\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}}(X)\\preceq\\frac{\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\,. (2.12)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-116667-118172"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.I1.i2.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 118355,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 118747,
      "raw_sha256": "2adf56f6988c2ace9a6c38a1c702b0e425e44304973cd3a027e9870c0f3068ed",
      "lf_sha256": "2adf56f6988c2ace9a6c38a1c702b0e425e44304973cd3a027e9870c0f3068ed",
      "source_text": "The Y -marginal potential satisfies",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.I1.i2.p1.1"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E13",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 118748,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 120244,
      "raw_sha256": "4f6cbd321e24190b27ea072854778d84c8ba6fe379ec56dae884115e04559cfc",
      "lf_sha256": "4f6cbd321e24190b27ea072854778d84c8ba6fe379ec56dae884115e04559cfc",
      "source_text": "\\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}U_{\\eta}(y)\\preceq\\frac{\\beta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\,. (2.13)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.E13"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-118811-120227",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 118811,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 120227,
      "raw_sha256": "863e423a971f4d3f0e7cc30e8ed35ce23315d2bbfd81715d982a507388a053c0",
      "lf_sha256": "863e423a971f4d3f0e7cc30e8ed35ce23315d2bbfd81715d982a507388a053c0",
      "source_text": "\\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha\\eta}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}U_{\\eta}(y)\\preceq\\frac{\\beta}{1+\\beta\\eta}I\\,. (2.13)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-118811-120227"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.I1.i3.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 120411,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 120544,
      "raw_sha256": "3134a4a4f9b962694a6a59571b298abdf3e44fa1412446b9b1d349e18b93a0ff",
      "lf_sha256": "3134a4a4f9b962694a6a59571b298abdf3e44fa1412446b9b1d349e18b93a0ff",
      "source_text": "The state-space reflection",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.I1.i3.p1.1"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E14",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Reflection symmetry is separate operator root, not curvature/marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 120545,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 121631,
      "raw_sha256": "9f6da2cb937646e03fb86a374e38fd8b61ca39cbcdc8306bd6aa89782fde8bb6",
      "lf_sha256": "9f6da2cb937646e03fb86a374e38fd8b61ca39cbcdc8306bd6aa89782fde8bb6",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}:(x,y)\\mapsto(x,2x-y) (2.14)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-120608-121614",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 120608,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 121614,
      "raw_sha256": "88297599ec553ecbb5f610274cede31c32face083ebc441896cc95e203d62cba",
      "lf_sha256": "88297599ec553ecbb5f610274cede31c32face083ebc441896cc95e203d62cba",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}:(x,y)\\mapsto(x,2x-y) (2.14)",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:byte-120608-121614"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.I1.i3.p1.2",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 121632,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 122066,
      "raw_sha256": "3a268ccc22610413f8d8af3ae8e6f52f635e8752d5fbadfd6346fa2d141fe321",
      "lf_sha256": "3a268ccc22610413f8d8af3ae8e6f52f635e8752d5fbadfd6346fa2d141fe321",
      "source_text": "preserves \\pi_{\\eta} and is an involution.",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.I1.i3.p1.2"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.SS2.p3.1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "NODE",
      "reason": "Source region within marginal-Poincare prerequisite/consumer slice.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 122137,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 125049,
      "raw_sha256": "cb3970f6f8fb24e28bec639bfe6a0c46cf83784b3134e6dab9e07337db24c18e",
      "lf_sha256": "cb3970f6f8fb24e28bec639bfe6a0c46cf83784b3134e6dab9e07337db24c18e",
      "source_text": "The Hessian bound in part (i) follows immediately from ( 1.1 ); the Poincaré and covariance bounds then follow from the standard log-concavity facts ( D.6 ) and Lemma D.3 in Appendix D , applied with m=\\alpha+\\eta^{-1} and L=\\beta+\\eta^{-1} . The marginal curvature bound in part (ii) is derived in Appendix D , at ( D.10 ). The reflection statement follows directly from ( 2.6 ).",
      "node_id": "pbps57:region:S2.SS2.p3.1"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.SS2.p4.1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Proximal/RGO algorithm convention or complexity motivation; not required for Eq2.13/D.6 marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 125095,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 125292,
      "raw_sha256": "7a34694fd20accfc20a2eaa3d3cd7dfd0d8e3e3b14e2644ce1602eecb757d627",
      "lf_sha256": "7a34694fd20accfc20a2eaa3d3cd7dfd0d8e3e3b14e2644ce1602eecb757d627",
      "source_text": "We use the standard proximal map convention of Moreau [ 24 ] :"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.E15",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Exact prox minimizer is analysis-only algorithm object, not marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 125293,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 127082,
      "raw_sha256": "6598bffc2f5ea1496c1b4308ed80f591895ec0ed56ec5ac3a6270863f24cc46d",
      "lf_sha256": "6598bffc2f5ea1496c1b4308ed80f591895ec0ed56ec5ac3a6270863f24cc46d",
      "source_text": "\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\coloneqq\\arg\\min_{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}}\\Bigl\\{V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,. (2.15)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-125356-127065",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Proximal/RGO algorithm convention or complexity motivation; not required for Eq2.13/D.6 marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 125356,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 127065,
      "raw_sha256": "a7ed211b4d0fd91e6ef187ab6ecfe9d6650aa2e0e9129c22229f169ff3f49b8b",
      "lf_sha256": "a7ed211b4d0fd91e6ef187ab6ecfe9d6650aa2e0e9129c22229f169ff3f49b8b",
      "source_text": "\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\coloneqq\\arg\\min_{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}}\\Bigl\\{V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^{2}}{2\\eta}\\Bigr\\}\\,. (2.15)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.SS2.p4.2",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Proximal/RGO algorithm convention or complexity motivation; not required for Eq2.13/D.6 marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 127083,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 129026,
      "raw_sha256": "03e60497f64847685185b27f99c2ade3cd690870e38f89d592481ff581ac2e4d",
      "lf_sha256": "03e60497f64847685185b27f99c2ade3cd690870e38f89d592481ff581ac2e4d",
      "source_text": "The minimizer is unique under ( 1.1 ). The objective minimized here is exactly the conditional potential ( 2.9 ), so \\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y) is the mode of \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} ; the conditional draw is in this sense a stochastic analogue of a proximal step, whence the terminology arises. This exact minimizer is used below only in the analysis; the implementable algorithm never evaluates it and does not assume access to a proximal oracle. We use the following conditional sampling primitive, introduced in [ 17 ] ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.Thmtheorem2",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "source-statement",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Proximal/RGO algorithm convention or complexity motivation; not required for Eq2.13/D.6 marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 129034,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 130545,
      "raw_sha256": "b82308ccee23ff7825c21760f156e93eeb18fb57a71ab5b4290d4c4f854613a7",
      "lf_sha256": "b82308ccee23ff7825c21760f156e93eeb18fb57a71ab5b4290d4c4f854613a7",
      "source_text": "Definition 2.2 (Restricted Gaussian oracle) . For \\eta>0 , a restricted Gaussian oracle (RGO) takes input y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d} and, using fresh randomness, returns a sample with law \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "S2.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Proximal/RGO algorithm convention or complexity motivation; not required for Eq2.13/D.6 marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 129492,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 130531,
      "raw_sha256": "f034803fea6e497674655f9ffc2a3f48bc782cad10cf4ca42d1d20be4e74aeb1",
      "lf_sha256": "f034803fea6e497674655f9ffc2a3f48bc782cad10cf4ca42d1d20be4e74aeb1",
      "source_text": "For \\eta>0 , a restricted Gaussian oracle (RGO) takes input y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d} and, using fresh randomness, returns a sample with law \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 708402,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 709830,
      "raw_sha256": "de79c8dd5844db921c4f71490d7daa454f3fc8929f26b00e4a271a5d402293fb",
      "lf_sha256": "de79c8dd5844db921c4f71490d7daa454f3fc8929f26b00e4a271a5d402293fb",
      "source_text": "Our target distribution is the joint law \\pi_{\\eta} defined in ( 2.6 ), and we set \\mathfrak{H}\\coloneqq L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}) . Recall from ( 3.11 ) that the ideal Proximal BPS has transition kernel"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 709831,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 712762,
      "raw_sha256": "9707a46ee18a8b8cb54a32f66af76ccfc32f733a3c7c2912a3a6bae2704ae18d",
      "lf_sha256": "9707a46ee18a8b8cb54a32f66af76ccfc32f733a3c7c2912a3a6bae2704ae18d",
      "source_text": "\\mathcal{K}\\bigl((x,y),\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime}\\bigr)=\\delta_{2x-y}(\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime})\\,\\bigl[\\rho\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y^{\\prime}}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})+(1-\\rho)\\,\\mathcal{H}_{y^{\\prime}}(x,\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})\\bigr]\\,,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-709894-712745",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 709894,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 712745,
      "raw_sha256": "84c65f41f83c3f5dbaa83e56f6225f47d85dde933f0a6d1257f226a4d9890613",
      "lf_sha256": "84c65f41f83c3f5dbaa83e56f6225f47d85dde933f0a6d1257f226a4d9890613",
      "source_text": "\\mathcal{K}\\bigl((x,y),\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime}\\bigr)=\\delta_{2x-y}(\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime})\\,\\bigl[\\rho\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y^{\\prime}}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})+(1-\\rho)\\,\\mathcal{H}_{y^{\\prime}}(x,\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})\\bigr]\\,,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p1.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 712763,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 713702,
      "raw_sha256": "b3e035b54388be180fe548bf263d024e320aaecb87bbb89f61872515b30e398a",
      "lf_sha256": "b3e035b54388be180fe548bf263d024e320aaecb87bbb89f61872515b30e398a",
      "source_text": "where \\mathcal{H}_{y^{\\prime}} is the conditional half-turn kernel from Proposition 3.2 . Since the algorithm is a discrete-time chain, its evolution is described by the induced one-step Markov operator on observables,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 713703,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 715721,
      "raw_sha256": "4f8753babcb60c32785aee89014fca6034ad8209dafe0adb4d9d7a8301dcaedc",
      "lf_sha256": "4f8753babcb60c32785aee89014fca6034ad8209dafe0adb4d9d7a8301dcaedc",
      "source_text": "(\\mathsf{K}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{2d}}f(x^{\\prime},y^{\\prime})\\,\\mathcal{K}\\bigl((x,y),\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime}\\bigr)\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-713766-715704",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 713766,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 715704,
      "raw_sha256": "a9d618b7f66cfeed29adf28047e3426aa0468e7d88bea61f5fd1187cd9270cd2",
      "lf_sha256": "a9d618b7f66cfeed29adf28047e3426aa0468e7d88bea61f5fd1187cd9270cd2",
      "source_text": "(\\mathsf{K}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{2d}}f(x^{\\prime},y^{\\prime})\\,\\mathcal{K}\\bigl((x,y),\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}y^{\\prime}\\bigr)\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p1.3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 715722,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 717552,
      "raw_sha256": "29dcbaba4a06509aae977b54a73bb5cb2aa358d3332b47485c7856e21fac6c3f",
      "lf_sha256": "29dcbaba4a06509aae977b54a73bb5cb2aa358d3332b47485c7856e21fac6c3f",
      "source_text": "Thus \\mathcal{K} acts on probability laws, whereas \\mathsf{K} is its induced action on observables. The first term in brackets in \\mathcal{K} is the conditional resampling branch. After the auxiliary coordinate is updated to y^{\\prime} , this branch replaces the x -coordinate by an independent draw from \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y^{\\prime}} . The associated conditional expectation operator is"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 717553,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 719703,
      "raw_sha256": "1f2c060d3d5cadb913d3707396a03d12fcbee241933e4bdc134beac774b8f18f",
      "lf_sha256": "1f2c060d3d5cadb913d3707396a03d12fcbee241933e4bdc134beac774b8f18f",
      "source_text": "(\\mathsf{P}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int f(x^{\\prime},y)\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})=\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y=y]\\,. (B.1)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-717615-719686",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 717615,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 719686,
      "raw_sha256": "edf7164aee5290e20227a7aa2550ed957d5307ccd7d9e6fa38351a2b0b7ee802",
      "lf_sha256": "edf7164aee5290e20227a7aa2550ed957d5307ccd7d9e6fa38351a2b0b7ee802",
      "source_text": "(\\mathsf{P}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq\\int f(x^{\\prime},y)\\,\\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y}(\\mathrm{d}x^{\\prime})=\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y=y]\\,. (B.1)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p1.4",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 719704,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 720476,
      "raw_sha256": "a315656fb855944b558eea0d3a8afbc9be4b177758fe77050b88170d7101fd1f",
      "lf_sha256": "a315656fb855944b558eea0d3a8afbc9be4b177758fe77050b88170d7101fd1f",
      "source_text": "In particular, \\mathsf{P}f depends only on the coordinate y . The range and kernel of \\mathsf{P} are"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 720477,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 724025,
      "raw_sha256": "2a3ed85e38715b4d6c91c8dbfb4a485c159c4511ad42beaded2a796d4bcdf30b",
      "lf_sha256": "2a3ed85e38715b4d6c91c8dbfb4a485c159c4511ad42beaded2a796d4bcdf30b",
      "source_text": "\\begin{split}\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:f(x,y)=g(y)\\text{ for some }g\\in L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})\\}\\,,\\\\ \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\ker(\\mathsf{P})=\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y]=0\\}\\,.\\end{split} (B.2)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-720539-724008",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 720539,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 724008,
      "raw_sha256": "ad164d707ae3886293bffcc209cc95ae1eb9edd53a3badcd8d898b50b515ec93",
      "lf_sha256": "ad164d707ae3886293bffcc209cc95ae1eb9edd53a3badcd8d898b50b515ec93",
      "source_text": "\\begin{split}\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:f(x,y)=g(y)\\text{ for some }g\\in L^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}^{Y})\\}\\,,\\\\ \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\ker(\\mathsf{P})=\\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp})=\\{f\\in\\mathfrak{H}:\\mathbb{E}[f(X,Y)\\mid Y]=0\\}\\,.\\end{split} (B.2)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p1.5",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 724026,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 727698,
      "raw_sha256": "45a62848de7e216745ebf2fffa52c1e6b51e25cf719343534bd1379105e287ca",
      "lf_sha256": "45a62848de7e216745ebf2fffa52c1e6b51e25cf719343534bd1379105e287ca",
      "source_text": "Here \\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\coloneqq I-\\mathsf{P} , so \\mathfrak{H}=\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} and f=\\mathsf{P}f+\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}f . In the common terminology of hypocoercivity [ 14 , 21 ] , \\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}) is the macroscopic subspace and its orthogonal complement is the microscopic subspace. Thus functions in \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} depend only on the coordinate y , whereas functions in \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} have zero mean under \\pi_{\\eta}^{X\\mid Y=y} for \\pi_{\\eta}^{Y} -almost every y ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p2.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 727744,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 728701,
      "raw_sha256": "67a249823a45d0791d380d82502de008221c5764091732d832022f730dfaa5a2",
      "lf_sha256": "67a249823a45d0791d380d82502de008221c5764091732d832022f730dfaa5a2",
      "source_text": "Relative to the decomposition \\mathfrak{H}=\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} , we write an operator \\mathsf{T} on \\mathfrak{H} in block form as"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 728702,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 732443,
      "raw_sha256": "7cb41b24f384991a849eef67e263bfcf9b3b2903b8a6c8dbef78020da9beb8b2",
      "lf_sha256": "7cb41b24f384991a849eef67e263bfcf9b3b2903b8a6c8dbef78020da9beb8b2",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{T}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\begin{aligned} \\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,,\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,.\\end{aligned} (B.3)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-728764-732426",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 728764,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 732426,
      "raw_sha256": "c263ca226b87c49711db1f4abf44e13ace41e780ad3cab2e6dbd508d9b4e4f77",
      "lf_sha256": "c263ca226b87c49711db1f4abf44e13ace41e780ad3cab2e6dbd508d9b4e4f77",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{T}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\begin{aligned} \\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\mathsf{P}\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,,\\\\ \\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}\\,,&\\mathsf{T}_{\\perp\\perp}&\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{T}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\,.\\end{aligned} (B.3)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p2.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 732444,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 733588,
      "raw_sha256": "28889578b27b023a0ae1d16736de10d47a78a137f3a7adbcc6d324152ef56123",
      "lf_sha256": "28889578b27b023a0ae1d16736de10d47a78a137f3a7adbcc6d324152ef56123",
      "source_text": "The first subscript specifies the target subspace and the second the source subspace; thus \\mathsf{T}_{ab}:\\mathfrak{H}_{b}\\to\\mathfrak{H}_{a} for a,b\\in\\{\\mathsf{P},\\perp\\} ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p3.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 733634,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 734350,
      "raw_sha256": "1409ebfb559525e9f9847fb391a418e0138bad9a1dbc5118f14ab4c7b7a02c6d",
      "lf_sha256": "1409ebfb559525e9f9847fb391a418e0138bad9a1dbc5118f14ab4c7b7a02c6d",
      "source_text": "We first apply this block notation to the reflection map \\mathsf{U} from ( 2.14 ). We use the same symbol for its pullback on observables:"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E4",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 734351,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 735917,
      "raw_sha256": "bd93f2e460e4f59aa562b2ba13e36ad16cd810424677c8b114e6a93474fc65b8",
      "lf_sha256": "bd93f2e460e4f59aa562b2ba13e36ad16cd810424677c8b114e6a93474fc65b8",
      "source_text": "(\\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq f(\\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\\,. (B.4)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-734413-735900",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 734413,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 735900,
      "raw_sha256": "695f01fc9d9038e82a9dabfa3e83e089938b4c043f67f0e730ae5b7d86d54b0b",
      "lf_sha256": "695f01fc9d9038e82a9dabfa3e83e089938b4c043f67f0e730ae5b7d86d54b0b",
      "source_text": "(\\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq f(\\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\\,. (B.4)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p3.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 735918,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 736025,
      "raw_sha256": "95381bf692de9064ad70901c44c1d2bde7d30e78835343c948ed1c85836d3edd",
      "lf_sha256": "95381bf692de9064ad70901c44c1d2bde7d30e78835343c948ed1c85836d3edd",
      "source_text": "This pullback is self-adjoint and unitary, and hence has block matrix"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 736026,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 737397,
      "raw_sha256": "641be5b1d1b759ebfba3960248023622f9c8632002f15921e7b60c7be7aeca67",
      "lf_sha256": "641be5b1d1b759ebfba3960248023622f9c8632002f15921e7b60c7be7aeca67",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\\\ \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-736089-737380",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 736089,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 737380,
      "raw_sha256": "c497429e1850fbad3dadcc6c6f3ca056c8bfe465afb034235a71ee2494d3c8d9",
      "lf_sha256": "c497429e1850fbad3dadcc6c6f3ca056c8bfe465afb034235a71ee2494d3c8d9",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\\\ \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p3.3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 737398,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 740262,
      "raw_sha256": "8a11ce1fbced31355991211c33dcb5681015fa2cb41e4b1f2585e566eddec354",
      "lf_sha256": "8a11ce1fbced31355991211c33dcb5681015fa2cb41e4b1f2585e566eddec354",
      "source_text": "Here \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to itself, whereas \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} . Since \\mathsf{U} is self-adjoint and unitary, \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} is a self-adjoint contraction on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} . Writing \\mathsf{U}^{2}=I in blocks gives"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E5",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 740263,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 742291,
      "raw_sha256": "fe258f4f7d272a57a2fa1293a3b4663924b5a3e556f87f1ce03cd28a3837f959",
      "lf_sha256": "fe258f4f7d272a57a2fa1293a3b4663924b5a3e556f87f1ce03cd28a3837f959",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,. (B.5)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-740325-742274",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 740325,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 742274,
      "raw_sha256": "9e26a9a7d7f947bf1d5a2a7841a47f1471a555d2060cc7b489a9cf813d7d614b",
      "lf_sha256": "9e26a9a7d7f947bf1d5a2a7841a47f1471a555d2060cc7b489a9cf813d7d614b",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,. (B.5)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p4.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 742337,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 748507,
      "raw_sha256": "0707d88742f77d60bf4954a0337425858975ee9b6777ddf2b85a38422a46b70b",
      "lf_sha256": "0707d88742f77d60bf4954a0337425858975ee9b6777ddf2b85a38422a46b70b",
      "source_text": "We next express the joint half-turn operator \\mathsf{H} in the same block decomposition. It is defined in ( A.9 ) and is a self-adjoint Markov contraction by Proposition A.2 . Since \\mathsf{H} acts only on the x -coordinate, while every function in \\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{P}) depends only on y , we have \\mathsf{H}\\mathsf{P}=\\mathsf{P} . Self-adjointness also gives \\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{H}=\\mathsf{P} . Set \\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{H}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}:\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}\\to\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} . The identity \\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{H}=\\mathsf{P} makes \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} invariant under \\mathsf{H} , so \\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp} is its restriction to \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} . It is therefore self-adjoint, and \\|\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}g\\|=\\|\\mathsf{H}g\\|\\leq\\|g\\| for g\\in\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} . Consequently,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E6",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 748508,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 749884,
      "raw_sha256": "6fdb7df30a1d6ca2b071447143072e8b72296176706d1858d80ff4a2da5c080d",
      "lf_sha256": "6fdb7df30a1d6ca2b071447143072e8b72296176706d1858d80ff4a2da5c080d",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{H}=\\mathsf{P}+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt-I\\preceq\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\preceq I\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}\\,. (B.6)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-748570-749867",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 748570,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 749867,
      "raw_sha256": "d4dd173afc33fc034199dd7c57c2e47f1bf819ea700bc71ad742067932a6f675",
      "lf_sha256": "d4dd173afc33fc034199dd7c57c2e47f1bf819ea700bc71ad742067932a6f675",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{H}=\\mathsf{P}+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt-I\\preceq\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\preceq I\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}\\,. (B.6)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p4.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 749885,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 750419,
      "raw_sha256": "dbf22baa129f4c1585d8c559bc7e191c7e162121292bb05e1e17f6363c915153",
      "lf_sha256": "dbf22baa129f4c1585d8c559bc7e191c7e162121292bb05e1e17f6363c915153",
      "source_text": "Relative to \\mathfrak{H}=\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} , this decomposition has the block representation"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex4",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 750420,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 751517,
      "raw_sha256": "fe5b6e14b7e55c6f8747244d2a14b5b4acf365ec816792b5f32f425cbfb37529",
      "lf_sha256": "fe5b6e14b7e55c6f8747244d2a14b5b4acf365ec816792b5f32f425cbfb37529",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{H}=\\begin{pmatrix}I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}}&0\\\\ 0&\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-750483-751500",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 750483,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 751500,
      "raw_sha256": "cbfff21b1e62c2f2abb45e5bef76f7a2504fa5103f672ab66e94e5efec46e67b",
      "lf_sha256": "cbfff21b1e62c2f2abb45e5bef76f7a2504fa5103f672ab66e94e5efec46e67b",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{H}=\\begin{pmatrix}I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}}&0\\\\ 0&\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p4.3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 751518,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 752076,
      "raw_sha256": "091aaca6015c184122846ea8d619a55642da05b1a88537985be1fc207304ecda",
      "lf_sha256": "091aaca6015c184122846ea8d619a55642da05b1a88537985be1fc207304ecda",
      "source_text": "The Markov operator \\mathsf{K} induced by the transition kernel \\mathcal{K} therefore factors as"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E7",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 752077,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 753899,
      "raw_sha256": "ee598301cbedfeacda43427f2983a592b4fd2c9bbeea7ad1f4aa798677f78139",
      "lf_sha256": "ee598301cbedfeacda43427f2983a592b4fd2c9bbeea7ad1f4aa798677f78139",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{K}=\\mathsf{U}\\bigl[\\rho\\mathsf{P}+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}\\bigr]=\\mathsf{U}\\bigl[\\mathsf{P}+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\bigr]\\,. (B.7)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-752139-753882",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 752139,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 753882,
      "raw_sha256": "88b255e74c1513f85048b87f7ebbeb82e4f2b1a3735c7230c2f3880164af4a80",
      "lf_sha256": "88b255e74c1513f85048b87f7ebbeb82e4f2b1a3735c7230c2f3880164af4a80",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{K}=\\mathsf{U}\\bigl[\\rho\\mathsf{P}+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}\\bigr]=\\mathsf{U}\\bigl[\\mathsf{P}+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\bigr]\\,. (B.7)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p4.4",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 753900,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 753978,
      "raw_sha256": "124acf1ab07d70e95e14b5738ed544900c3d2533695f8a65bf70d7b9d5cac37f",
      "lf_sha256": "124acf1ab07d70e95e14b5738ed544900c3d2533695f8a65bf70d7b9d5cac37f",
      "source_text": "Accordingly, its block representation is"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex5",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 753979,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 756113,
      "raw_sha256": "08d3db4d937c51127f2d9026668f07489237b992043b5b1265bdfe6026b460b3",
      "lf_sha256": "08d3db4d937c51127f2d9026668f07489237b992043b5b1265bdfe6026b460b3",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{K}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\\\ \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}}&0\\\\ 0&(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-754042-756096",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 754042,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 756096,
      "raw_sha256": "10fb92dda90eac87b04f4430eb6a8bd2e7ba09c1a97f603fa709361f39e8f4a7",
      "lf_sha256": "10fb92dda90eac87b04f4430eb6a8bd2e7ba09c1a97f603fa709361f39e8f4a7",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{K}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\\\ \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}}&0\\\\ 0&(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS1.p4.5",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS1",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Operator/half-turn framework downstream of scalar marginal PI; definitions retained as separate context roots, not hypotheses of marginal PI.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 756114,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 758352,
      "raw_sha256": "c9f9c546417ca85a01a56613cc7ae0584441dfbd7d79991f712744d00b9171e0",
      "lf_sha256": "c9f9c546417ca85a01a56613cc7ae0584441dfbd7d79991f712744d00b9171e0",
      "source_text": "The diagonal factor in the block representation of \\mathsf{K} contracts \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} but leaves \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} unchanged. For an observable f\\in\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} , contraction therefore relies on the \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} -component \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f created by reflection. The next subsection estimates this component and the subsequent action of \\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp} ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E8",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E8",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 762524,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 764253,
      "raw_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a",
      "lf_sha256": "5a60b7a7667ec1a06d63f370f1711890038e27cb223b63d17031494e7ee0928a",
      "source_text": "Y_{+}\\coloneqq X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\\coloneqq X-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptX\\sim\\mu\\,. (B.8)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-762586-764236",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E8",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 762586,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 764236,
      "raw_sha256": "a99bc85111524af04e4d41641203354c26404cffdc81386b53fd8177272308b8",
      "lf_sha256": "a99bc85111524af04e4d41641203354c26404cffdc81386b53fd8177272308b8",
      "source_text": "Y_{+}\\coloneqq X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\\coloneqq X-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,Z\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptZ\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptX\\sim\\mu\\,. (B.8)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E9",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E9",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 765724,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 768134,
      "raw_sha256": "d24fec695423a3d6af884a8a3fe3c46804b6e817f935fb89b1853a6ab5f65241",
      "lf_sha256": "d24fec695423a3d6af884a8a3fe3c46804b6e817f935fb89b1853a6ab5f65241",
      "source_text": "(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f)(y)=\\mathbb{E}[f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+}=y]\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\mathbb{E}\\Var(f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+})\\,. (B.9)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-765786-768117",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E9",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 765786,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 768117,
      "raw_sha256": "aea93eb6114c618ec7828fa8e36f81757d9fab7aa70c9b7d9dc4717b3dd8a702",
      "lf_sha256": "aea93eb6114c618ec7828fa8e36f81757d9fab7aa70c9b7d9dc4717b3dd8a702",
      "source_text": "(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f)(y)=\\mathbb{E}[f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+}=y]\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\mathbb{E}\\Var(f(Y_{-})\\mid Y_{+})\\,. (B.9)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E10",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E10",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 768975,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 770419,
      "raw_sha256": "7b09ee8258f3e6c4ecc506e9513ec8256e0d1f4083f38b545d6c1dd03486c0fb",
      "lf_sha256": "7b09ee8258f3e6c4ecc506e9513ec8256e0d1f4083f38b545d6c1dd03486c0fb",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,. (B.10)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-769038-770402",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E10",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 769038,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 770402,
      "raw_sha256": "1c2d9b6cb28ccc39a22809f2b7eb8e4e90ecd2598b538186a392530afb629400",
      "lf_sha256": "1c2d9b6cb28ccc39a22809f2b7eb8e4e90ecd2598b538186a392530afb629400",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,. (B.10)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E11",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E11",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 771531,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 773654,
      "raw_sha256": "6d19997456600e603e6f081f055bf929069a5e636c8c8fa7d2cb37a8615428f7",
      "lf_sha256": "6d19997456600e603e6f081f055bf929069a5e636c8c8fa7d2cb37a8615428f7",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f\\|\\,,\\hskip 10.00002ptf\\in\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,. (B.11)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-771594-773637",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E11",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 771594,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 773637,
      "raw_sha256": "995d4994c960372369d34a202475bbe1a21542b74e1077e191e7ef03d64f00bc",
      "lf_sha256": "995d4994c960372369d34a202475bbe1a21542b74e1077e191e7ef03d64f00bc",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f\\|\\,,\\hskip 10.00002ptf\\in\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,. (B.11)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E12",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E12",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 775053,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 776847,
      "raw_sha256": "7925618a142c1514a962d18e4c580f39fa4bc85426ba98de4c84a8b90e6bdc42",
      "lf_sha256": "7925618a142c1514a962d18e4c580f39fa4bc85426ba98de4c84a8b90e6bdc42",
      "source_text": "\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\coloneqq\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\gamma_{\\rm gap}\\coloneqq\\sqrt{1-\\rho_{\\rm mac}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,. (B.12)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-775116-776830",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E12",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 775116,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 776830,
      "raw_sha256": "f2bc8a9474377cb2e6794787f1eaad7356c9de28d10f49565d40add81959ad0f",
      "lf_sha256": "f2bc8a9474377cb2e6794787f1eaad7356c9de28d10f49565d40add81959ad0f",
      "source_text": "\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\coloneqq\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\gamma_{\\rm gap}\\coloneqq\\sqrt{1-\\rho_{\\rm mac}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\,. (B.12)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E13",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E13",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 778803,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 781042,
      "raw_sha256": "4c2b2e9e8eaa80d678ec267da6e0588623b414d073755a2ce4f675b151a8cfad",
      "lf_sha256": "4c2b2e9e8eaa80d678ec267da6e0588623b414d073755a2ce4f675b151a8cfad",
      "source_text": "4\\eta\\,\\|\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\leq\\|f\\|^{2}-\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\,. (B.13)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-778866-781025",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E13",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 778866,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 781025,
      "raw_sha256": "33da05f4a184184cea0a51482360dd541483a0f5d6ab79187c1c3218f41610b3",
      "lf_sha256": "33da05f4a184184cea0a51482360dd541483a0f5d6ab79187c1c3218f41610b3",
      "source_text": "4\\eta\\,\\|\\nabla\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\leq\\|f\\|^{2}-\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}=\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f\\|^{2}\\,. (B.13)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E14",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E14",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 781999,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 783825,
      "raw_sha256": "69957ed7951efb4ab6a2f23e1e8aee574c98defc2fec2e58b12a7d6a9209b498",
      "lf_sha256": "69957ed7951efb4ab6a2f23e1e8aee574c98defc2fec2e58b12a7d6a9209b498",
      "source_text": "\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\|\\leq\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{and}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq-\\frac{1}{2}\\,I\\hskip 20.00003pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\,. (B.14)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-782062-783808",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E14",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 782062,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 783808,
      "raw_sha256": "b86505d87b45ae7f4c80eb6aee9ed2c628e0259eacb42e6025b17e027f25ddc0",
      "lf_sha256": "b86505d87b45ae7f4c80eb6aee9ed2c628e0259eacb42e6025b17e027f25ddc0",
      "source_text": "\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\|\\leq\\rho_{\\rm mac}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\text{and}\\hskip 10.00002pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq-\\frac{1}{2}\\,I\\hskip 20.00003pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\,. (B.14)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E15",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E15",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 783959,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 785610,
      "raw_sha256": "0a85d657415c5c8dbb19e6014e528156f3ce5badc750e5849423f1f042da3ebf",
      "lf_sha256": "0a85d657415c5c8dbb19e6014e528156f3ce5badc750e5849423f1f042da3ebf",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}=(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\\succeq\\gamma_{\\rm gap}I\\hskip 20.00003pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\,. (B.15)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-784022-785593",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E15",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 784022,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 785593,
      "raw_sha256": "654589a51def6e610d2e75497cfcdceaa6128ee456a437f1993c28dcd32fd3dc",
      "lf_sha256": "654589a51def6e610d2e75497cfcdceaa6128ee456a437f1993c28dcd32fd3dc",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}=(I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\\succeq\\gamma_{\\rm gap}I\\hskip 20.00003pt\\text{on }\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\,. (B.15)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E16",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E16",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 790549,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 793315,
      "raw_sha256": "a6725987d1979361ae4770ec893b554213101161e297c456081d28b8ef5b9042",
      "lf_sha256": "a6725987d1979361ae4770ec893b554213101161e297c456081d28b8ef5b9042",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\,:\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\longrightarrow\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}}\\,. (B.16)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-790612-793298",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E16",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 790612,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 793298,
      "raw_sha256": "bb294eee4928e5a12aa2049c7a7062c386d761f925747ed8066bccc6084cffca",
      "lf_sha256": "bb294eee4928e5a12aa2049c7a7062c386d761f925747ed8066bccc6084cffca",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\,:\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\longrightarrow\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}}\\,. (B.16)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E17",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E17",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 796522,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 798813,
      "raw_sha256": "dbb70897bf5ef82c9a5b2a3e3d31d42e1c4b5d5daa9f4591899eb4e0dab3a73d",
      "lf_sha256": "dbb70897bf5ef82c9a5b2a3e3d31d42e1c4b5d5daa9f4591899eb4e0dab3a73d",
      "source_text": "\\bigl\\|(I+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp})\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}v\\bigr\\|^{2}\\leq C\\log(1/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})\\,\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}v\\|^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptv\\in\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\,. (B.17)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-796585-798796",
      "anchor_container": "A2.E17",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Gamma/block/gap/half-turn source equation belongs to a separate source root or downstream theorem; no marginal PI prerequisite.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 796585,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 798796,
      "raw_sha256": "39bfba34eda6be9f394dfe6cf11352c7e24954e2b82424a957161fa5b3dd9c35",
      "lf_sha256": "39bfba34eda6be9f394dfe6cf11352c7e24954e2b82424a957161fa5b3dd9c35",
      "source_text": "\\bigl\\|(I+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp})\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}v\\bigr\\|^{2}\\leq C\\log(1/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})\\,\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}v\\|^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptv\\in\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\,. (B.17)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 801631,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 802756,
      "raw_sha256": "7aa2862479e8feceebf05f1a941dcdeba705947bcf5fed9e98dbc0c5b171cfb2",
      "lf_sha256": "7aa2862479e8feceebf05f1a941dcdeba705947bcf5fed9e98dbc0c5b171cfb2",
      "source_text": "We now prove Theorem 3.5 using a discrete modified L^{2} argument. For f\\in L_{0}^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}) , write"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex6",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 802757,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 803801,
      "raw_sha256": "62e11e7acaf86a3187ffcf4ba2a793b19677dc3c8c9bc55acad434435d7eb400",
      "lf_sha256": "62e11e7acaf86a3187ffcf4ba2a793b19677dc3c8c9bc55acad434435d7eb400",
      "source_text": "f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}f\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptf_{\\perp}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}f\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-802820-803784",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 802820,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 803784,
      "raw_sha256": "f1ec832ad181288bf1c3f15e9478220253d1b6eb8acfe233b6fa9254d11715aa",
      "lf_sha256": "f1ec832ad181288bf1c3f15e9478220253d1b6eb8acfe233b6fa9254d11715aa",
      "source_text": "f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}f\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptf_{\\perp}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}f\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p1.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 803802,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 804554,
      "raw_sha256": "c901ee0614e10b08f422a63a5b80fb473317eef17eee1a5b20fb36bf847376d6",
      "lf_sha256": "c901ee0614e10b08f422a63a5b80fb473317eef17eee1a5b20fb36bf847376d6",
      "source_text": "Here f_{\\mathsf{P}} and f_{\\perp} are, respectively, the macroscopic and microscopic parts of f ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p2.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 804600,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 805802,
      "raw_sha256": "f393d95fee9bf085549381f116783525e75ebbb646dbf9414eaba8929d3a724b",
      "lf_sha256": "f393d95fee9bf085549381f116783525e75ebbb646dbf9414eaba8929d3a724b",
      "source_text": "Fix 0<\\rho\\leq 1/2 . The ordinary L^{2} energy does not by itself give the required one-step contraction. Indeed, since \\mathsf{U} is unitary and \\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp} is a contraction,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-805898-807717",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 805898,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 807717,
      "raw_sha256": "81d2508da643d310e3d0b0e486e7b4fe3270bba4e382d6c866414e4fb8593297",
      "lf_sha256": "81d2508da643d310e3d0b0e486e7b4fe3270bba4e382d6c866414e4fb8593297",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle\\|\\mathsf{K}f\\|^{2}-\\|f\\|^{2} \\displaystyle=(1-\\rho)^{2}\\,\\|\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}-\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-807745-809184",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 807745,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 809184,
      "raw_sha256": "bfe448f8418ad638aef4778b8a3a9360a48b76d154b5c2f7f63e0ccc1c33d8f7",
      "lf_sha256": "bfe448f8418ad638aef4778b8a3a9360a48b76d154b5c2f7f63e0ccc1c33d8f7",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle\\leq-\\rho\\,(2-\\rho)\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\leq-\\rho\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\,. (B.18)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p2.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 809202,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 812143,
      "raw_sha256": "f7371a45cbcef4096739d91bb520e604a5215bf7abfe90431957bb215f4cd53b",
      "lf_sha256": "f7371a45cbcef4096739d91bb520e604a5215bf7abfe90431957bb215f4cd53b",
      "source_text": "This estimate controls f_{\\perp} but gives nothing when f=f_{\\mathsf{P}} . Reflection moves part of f_{\\mathsf{P}} into the microscopic subspace, but this transfer is not captured by the L^{2} norm, which is a standard difficulty in hypocoercivity. The modified L^{2} method addresses this difficulty by adding a corrector to the Lyapunov function. The corrector records the transfer from f_{\\mathsf{P}} to f_{\\perp} , allowing the contraction in ( B.18 ) to also control f_{\\mathsf{P}} . This idea goes back to Dolbeault, Mouhot, and Schmeiser [ 14 ] ; here we follow the refinement of Fan, Li, and Lu [ 16 ] ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p3.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 812189,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 812785,
      "raw_sha256": "0d94733a14625e30597bdea2f8a797c65e633acee15b0483bb75a7d5cd5c956e",
      "lf_sha256": "0d94733a14625e30597bdea2f8a797c65e633acee15b0483bb75a7d5cd5c956e",
      "source_text": "To construct the corrector, we first isolate the part of f_{\\perp} that couples to f_{\\mathsf{P}} under reflection. Define"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex8",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 812786,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 813671,
      "raw_sha256": "26df72e0ccc629a8ec711eb2f1926260341e84661daefbf9d260c42cc747d1f5",
      "lf_sha256": "26df72e0ccc629a8ec711eb2f1926260341e84661daefbf9d260c42cc747d1f5",
      "source_text": "f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\\perp}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-812849-813654",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 812849,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 813654,
      "raw_sha256": "7e1313412cafd57400469687b22c21be1b1ae9c41693ca524586f25d34236f08",
      "lf_sha256": "7e1313412cafd57400469687b22c21be1b1ae9c41693ca524586f25d34236f08",
      "source_text": "f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\\perp}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p3.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 813672,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 819450,
      "raw_sha256": "2ae1a006f3bfd3b33a654570286671c69b29eb27ae92c18d33232feabf05cc94",
      "lf_sha256": "2ae1a006f3bfd3b33a654570286671c69b29eb27ae92c18d33232feabf05cc94",
      "source_text": "By ( B.16 ), \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\\perp}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{V}} , while the component of f_{\\perp} orthogonal to \\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}) is annihilated by \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*} . Since \\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}} is an isometry, \\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{V}}=\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\\perp} is the orthogonal projection of f_{\\perp} onto \\operatorname{ran}(\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}) , and hence \\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|\\leq\\|f_{\\perp}\\| . We work with f_{\\mathsf{V}} , rather than with this projection itself, because f_{\\mathsf{V}} and f_{\\mathsf{P}} both belong to \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0} and can therefore be paired in the corrector."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p4.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 819496,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 819871,
      "raw_sha256": "81d72d159f0f3fbe1c416f72ac6559ebe8a2279651f4d0e6ad6cebc06acdf185",
      "lf_sha256": "81d72d159f0f3fbe1c416f72ac6559ebe8a2279651f4d0e6ad6cebc06acdf185",
      "source_text": "With this notation, let \\omega>0 be a weight to be chosen below and define the modified Lyapunov function"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E19",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 819872,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 821354,
      "raw_sha256": "73df15038489a3d88940290cc920bc8632d40c43648ea312581c76c34b0093e5",
      "lf_sha256": "73df15038489a3d88940290cc920bc8632d40c43648ea312581c76c34b0093e5",
      "source_text": "\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\coloneqq\\|f\\|^{2}+\\omega\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})\\,, (B.19)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-819935-821337",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 819935,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 821337,
      "raw_sha256": "bb0491ad0e9b27b358996bf61f51d378dda2e1c7bf2f6c72a0027637861440fd",
      "lf_sha256": "bb0491ad0e9b27b358996bf61f51d378dda2e1c7bf2f6c72a0027637861440fd",
      "source_text": "\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\coloneqq\\|f\\|^{2}+\\omega\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})\\,, (B.19)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p4.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 821355,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 821415,
      "raw_sha256": "82e9adf7b1d3e188272d24aaea11353ac83763a5a293c0a3c97d2b6fb46a4f4f",
      "lf_sha256": "82e9adf7b1d3e188272d24aaea11353ac83763a5a293c0a3c97d2b6fb46a4f4f",
      "source_text": "where the corrector is"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E20",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 821416,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 823817,
      "raw_sha256": "a9aeb59d4171f7729695c84c23ecd6f5533625c550517074564725865df77744",
      "lf_sha256": "a9aeb59d4171f7729695c84c23ecd6f5533625c550517074564725865df77744",
      "source_text": "\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})\\coloneqq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl(\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}-\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\bigr)-\\bigl\\langle\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\bigr\\rangle\\,. (B.20)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-821479-823800",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 821479,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 823800,
      "raw_sha256": "404d4eee05dbfd814bd5a180b9e039569bd83ef710636038b96d68ec3850bbf6",
      "lf_sha256": "404d4eee05dbfd814bd5a180b9e039569bd83ef710636038b96d68ec3850bbf6",
      "source_text": "\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})\\coloneqq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl(\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}-\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\bigr)-\\bigl\\langle\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\bigr\\rangle\\,. (B.20)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p4.3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 823818,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 825089,
      "raw_sha256": "6b642d6ccd24e7b36165cc682ba1eaf604f04fe6d4262fe2b712bc23757c91c9",
      "lf_sha256": "6b642d6ccd24e7b36165cc682ba1eaf604f04fe6d4262fe2b712bc23757c91c9",
      "source_text": "Here \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1} is applied only on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0} , where \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq\\gamma_{\\rm gap}I , so the corrector is well-defined."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 825135,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 825783,
      "raw_sha256": "fa8f6782156ab262906a9d14e7161d2fa3df01304b3794cce44544a1e67db959",
      "lf_sha256": "fa8f6782156ab262906a9d14e7161d2fa3df01304b3794cce44544a1e67db959",
      "source_text": "To motivate this choice, recall from ( B.7 ) that \\mathsf{K} acts in two stages: it first maps"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex9",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 825784,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 826951,
      "raw_sha256": "0aac0704e07a536fb95d755fe34cc16b020a7784233b60bd836e6a93c95c4a1d",
      "lf_sha256": "0aac0704e07a536fb95d755fe34cc16b020a7784233b60bd836e6a93c95c4a1d",
      "source_text": "f_{\\mathsf{P}}+f_{\\perp}\\longmapsto f_{\\mathsf{P}}+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}f_{\\perp}"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-825847-826934",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 825847,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 826934,
      "raw_sha256": "ee931d3c815d28adf42bb9d070f9c7c3b95fff3fa89c124c666c0a70ddfeb397",
      "lf_sha256": "ee931d3c815d28adf42bb9d070f9c7c3b95fff3fa89c124c666c0a70ddfeb397",
      "source_text": "f_{\\mathsf{P}}+f_{\\perp}\\longmapsto f_{\\mathsf{P}}+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}f_{\\perp}"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 826952,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 828957,
      "raw_sha256": "e9353f75c4d47dbf285a8398d3f0615a4654f1589a29640a57b33a03db40f798",
      "lf_sha256": "e9353f75c4d47dbf285a8398d3f0615a4654f1589a29640a57b33a03db40f798",
      "source_text": "and then applies \\mathsf{U} . For the moment, set \\rho=0 and replace \\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp} by -I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}} . The error I+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp} introduced by this replacement is controlled by Proposition B.2 . Denote the resulting idealized operator by"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex10",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 828958,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 829852,
      "raw_sha256": "7edfd995a7423e2b3ad8654f6cbba12d918e85d748877ffeba4ae7500cc36048",
      "lf_sha256": "7edfd995a7423e2b3ad8654f6cbba12d918e85d748877ffeba4ae7500cc36048",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{U}(\\mathsf{P}-\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp})\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-829022-829835",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 829022,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 829835,
      "raw_sha256": "785c24fa128d15113f87ef9bcb5c8869bfe33edef299c64ce34ea8bd890d2d19",
      "lf_sha256": "785c24fa128d15113f87ef9bcb5c8869bfe33edef299c64ce34ea8bd890d2d19",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{U}(\\mathsf{P}-\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp})\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 829853,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 830303,
      "raw_sha256": "e2f000707c436421bb0c32e47f920b119778db81b8f7727bcf2932711fa68d33",
      "lf_sha256": "e2f000707c436421bb0c32e47f920b119778db81b8f7727bcf2932711fa68d33",
      "source_text": "Set g\\coloneqq\\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id}f , and define the corresponding components by"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex11",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 830304,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 831566,
      "raw_sha256": "c5f25ac21eaabc3eaecc999def77a9b4a5581d9c34f47ec0b7b5492d4db671be",
      "lf_sha256": "c5f25ac21eaabc3eaecc999def77a9b4a5581d9c34f47ec0b7b5492d4db671be",
      "source_text": "g_{\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}g\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptg_{\\mathsf{V}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}g\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-830368-831549",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 830368,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 831549,
      "raw_sha256": "2b1663643c44f90e74e6cb7ad5e194feb41d8c1c09357d994b7ef06b1c457796",
      "lf_sha256": "2b1663643c44f90e74e6cb7ad5e194feb41d8c1c09357d994b7ef06b1c457796",
      "source_text": "g_{\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}g\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptg_{\\mathsf{V}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}g\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.4",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 831567,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 831935,
      "raw_sha256": "79f58c7d8fd19dae11d81ab3d68b0ab31b7de54572670f1027f5ca2585e17c41",
      "lf_sha256": "79f58c7d8fd19dae11d81ab3d68b0ab31b7de54572670f1027f5ca2585e17c41",
      "source_text": "In terms of these components, \\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id} is represented by the operator-valued rotation matrix"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex12",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 831936,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 833969,
      "raw_sha256": "e788e16052769191b322569deeaf1320a9391be2df127c5286f66316a131615f",
      "lf_sha256": "e788e16052769191b322569deeaf1320a9391be2df127c5286f66316a131615f",
      "source_text": "\\begin{pmatrix}g_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ g_{\\mathsf{V}}\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&-\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-832000-833952",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 832000,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 833952,
      "raw_sha256": "8b746a738adaaf73f6b9048b682f0cbe71c8e299aa89083132993ec5919dcb55",
      "lf_sha256": "8b746a738adaaf73f6b9048b682f0cbe71c8e299aa89083132993ec5919dcb55",
      "source_text": "\\begin{pmatrix}g_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ g_{\\mathsf{V}}\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&-\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.5",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 833970,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 834657,
      "raw_sha256": "ba0974601c2289e21858be7eb9b156d87f826dc8f46a1c42ba8707ab94974f72",
      "lf_sha256": "ba0974601c2289e21858be7eb9b156d87f826dc8f46a1c42ba8707ab94974f72",
      "source_text": "Indeed, the first component follows immediately from the block representation of \\mathsf{U} and the polar decomposition ( B.16 ):"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-834754-837662",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 834754,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 837662,
      "raw_sha256": "0f659e2c774faa4f3432ee15979a6e45e9ce48c9d519fdcde00c369bf51f3893",
      "lf_sha256": "0f659e2c774faa4f3432ee15979a6e45e9ce48c9d519fdcde00c369bf51f3893",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle g_{\\mathsf{P}} \\displaystyle=\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{U}(f_{\\mathsf{P}}-f_{\\perp})=\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{P}}-\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\\perp}=\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{P}}-\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\\perp}=\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{P}}-\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.6",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 837680,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 840375,
      "raw_sha256": "fa75e62c8ca38292893d594c5c8cf776915def4e4b0a0c96c393b39c19c83aea",
      "lf_sha256": "fa75e62c8ca38292893d594c5c8cf776915def4e4b0a0c96c393b39c19c83aea",
      "source_text": "For the second component, substitute \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*} into \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*} from ( B.5 ). Since \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} commutes with \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}} , this gives"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex14",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 840376,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 841998,
      "raw_sha256": "d90dafd45d71ab6e9b622991c01bf32eb29251bccfe258b3934042fad812ca3f",
      "lf_sha256": "d90dafd45d71ab6e9b622991c01bf32eb29251bccfe258b3934042fad812ca3f",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-840440-841981",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 840440,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 841981,
      "raw_sha256": "64c3b0c4d05273b57647a8544e16fb1d061c33f9b1cd0d107f9e1bda0eb68d4a",
      "lf_sha256": "64c3b0c4d05273b57647a8544e16fb1d061c33f9b1cd0d107f9e1bda0eb68d4a",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.7",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 841999,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 845119,
      "raw_sha256": "b5d4f7bc368d0eaae71b7bf078b64de3a84fcb7b5aa0ce826f20a506c1c887d6",
      "lf_sha256": "b5d4f7bc368d0eaae71b7bf078b64de3a84fcb7b5aa0ce826f20a506c1c887d6",
      "source_text": "The ranges of \\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp} and \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*} lie in \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0} , where \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1} is bounded. Applying \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1} to the displayed identity therefore gives \\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*} . Hence"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-845216-848727",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 845216,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 848727,
      "raw_sha256": "a7ad262dbaf2c188fcba1fbe34beec9902a186b472331a6328e3d7ffa127a443",
      "lf_sha256": "a7ad262dbaf2c188fcba1fbe34beec9902a186b472331a6328e3d7ffa127a443",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle g_{\\mathsf{V}} \\displaystyle=\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{U}(f_{\\mathsf{P}}-f_{\\perp})=\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}(\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{P}}-\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}f_{\\perp})=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{P}}+\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\\perp}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{P}}+\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.8",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 848745,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 850266,
      "raw_sha256": "206594cc7dd50d26f8bad1d70ede17b21cd9b4fe594d2f38227e87eca8509b60",
      "lf_sha256": "206594cc7dd50d26f8bad1d70ede17b21cd9b4fe594d2f38227e87eca8509b60",
      "source_text": "This proves the claimed matrix formula. Since \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I , the block matrix acts as a rotation on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0}\\oplus\\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0} . Under this rotation, direct substitution into ( B.20 ) gives"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-850363-851444",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 850363,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 851444,
      "raw_sha256": "548d38230a101615d2e3cd1a0f33e47a23bb2dd66d4f9d65b2b7f38c8d8c00de",
      "lf_sha256": "548d38230a101615d2e3cd1a0f33e47a23bb2dd66d4f9d65b2b7f38c8d8c00de",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle\\mathscr{C}(g_{\\mathsf{P}},g_{\\mathsf{V}})-\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-851473-853563",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 851473,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 853563,
      "raw_sha256": "e630cda9024090690060a889af9fed6d938091441820756d549a3414b3f61707",
      "lf_sha256": "e630cda9024090690060a889af9fed6d938091441820756d549a3414b3f61707",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle\\hskip 10.00002pt=\\mathscr{C}(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{P}}-\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\,,\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{P}}+\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}f_{\\mathsf{V}})-\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-853591-854742",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 853591,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 854742,
      "raw_sha256": "6db8355bcb41b7767b5309207f4387dff71016b42016da1beed1712cf7f60851",
      "lf_sha256": "6db8355bcb41b7767b5309207f4387dff71016b42016da1beed1712cf7f60851",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle\\hskip 10.00002pt=-\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\,. (B.21)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.9",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 854760,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 856300,
      "raw_sha256": "3a1c4bbcc44632b2a58db4fd30eb46c4f8d61627bdbbb58aa9b7dbed6a66354c",
      "lf_sha256": "3a1c4bbcc44632b2a58db4fd30eb46c4f8d61627bdbbb58aa9b7dbed6a66354c",
      "source_text": "For 0<\\omega<\\rho , combining the leading terms from ( B.18 ) and ( B.21 ), and using \\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|\\leq\\|f_{\\perp}\\| , gives"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-856398-858492",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 856398,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 858492,
      "raw_sha256": "5964fcdd96e2241ca8e2d8f1de323a5ca812b79490ff2a561de19ec6a653e84a",
      "lf_sha256": "5964fcdd96e2241ca8e2d8f1de323a5ca812b79490ff2a561de19ec6a653e84a",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle-\\rho\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}+\\omega\\,\\bigl(-\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\bigr)\\leq-\\omega\\,\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}-(\\rho-\\omega)\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p5.10",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 858510,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 859042,
      "raw_sha256": "476ebdbf6dddf1031f52b257a972111744404aab30f9844e678cd0303618b0f2",
      "lf_sha256": "476ebdbf6dddf1031f52b257a972111744404aab30f9844e678cd0303618b0f2",
      "source_text": "Thus the leading terms control both components. This calculation makes explicit the role of the corrector in the modified L^{2} hypocoercivity argument; see also Fan, Li, and Lu [ 16 ] ."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p6.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 859088,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 859775,
      "raw_sha256": "a4625dbde27b92c737b14af4c4f0529b6b225ad5c993ae5d5e93fbf1cbc74e70",
      "lf_sha256": "a4625dbde27b92c737b14af4c4f0529b6b225ad5c993ae5d5e93fbf1cbc74e70",
      "source_text": "We now turn from the idealized calculation to the contraction proof. The modified L^{2} argument has two steps: we first show that the Lyapunov function is equivalent to the squared L^{2} norm and then establish its one-step decay."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Thmtheorem3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "source-statement",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 859783,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 862853,
      "raw_sha256": "365ca267d2697fea1bfd5064688efc9020a52a9aa08cb36b7d95c7483fc49101",
      "lf_sha256": "365ca267d2697fea1bfd5064688efc9020a52a9aa08cb36b7d95c7483fc49101",
      "source_text": "Lemma B.3 (Equivalence with the squared L^{2} norm) . If 0<\\omega\\leq\\gamma_{\\rm gap} , then every f\\in L_{0}^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}) satisfies \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\leq\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\leq\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,. (B.22)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 860458,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 861407,
      "raw_sha256": "50364ab5f471370d50114941b2f7bed8e6cd2556acfb32a681e04b17a869311e",
      "lf_sha256": "50364ab5f471370d50114941b2f7bed8e6cd2556acfb32a681e04b17a869311e",
      "source_text": "If 0<\\omega\\leq\\gamma_{\\rm gap} , then every f\\in L_{0}^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}) satisfies"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E22",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 861408,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 862839,
      "raw_sha256": "bb6ecda78392cca9bc08c163c366ebdcc6065b7b8a1a86cd45eda430e14ca266",
      "lf_sha256": "bb6ecda78392cca9bc08c163c366ebdcc6065b7b8a1a86cd45eda430e14ca266",
      "source_text": "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\leq\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\leq\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,. (B.22)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-861471-862822",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 861471,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 862822,
      "raw_sha256": "509dbf6c6e2b65d22c049073f8fdb97a2da93ef7969bf79cc09b1e833e349be7",
      "lf_sha256": "509dbf6c6e2b65d22c049073f8fdb97a2da93ef7969bf79cc09b1e833e349be7",
      "source_text": "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\leq\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\leq\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,. (B.22)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "proof-container",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 862854,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 883202,
      "raw_sha256": "4195397b51300fd5f8143aec7f45c43086f35802c74d6f9bc6cc646a5670a488",
      "lf_sha256": "4195397b51300fd5f8143aec7f45c43086f35802c74d6f9bc6cc646a5670a488",
      "source_text": "Proof. The operators \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} and \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}} commute, so \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1} is self-adjoint on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0} . Moreover, I+(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1})^{2}=I+\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\\,, where the last identity uses \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I . By ( B.20 ), \\displaystyle 2\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}}) \\displaystyle=\\Bigl\\langle\\begin{pmatrix}f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\end{pmatrix}\\,,\\begin{pmatrix}I&-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\\\ -\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&-I\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\end{pmatrix}\\Bigr\\rangle\\,. The square of the block operator in this display is \\begin{pmatrix}I&-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\\\ -\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&-I\\end{pmatrix}^{\\!2}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}&0\\\\ 0&\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\\end{pmatrix}\\,. Since the block operator is self-adjoint and \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq\\gamma_{\\rm gap}I , \\Bigl\\|\\begin{pmatrix}I&-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\\\ -\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&-I\\end{pmatrix}\\Bigr\\|=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\|\\leq\\frac{1}{\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,. Applying this operator norm bound to the preceding quadratic form gives |\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})|\\leq\\frac{1}{2\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,\\bigl(\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\bigr)\\leq\\frac{1}{2\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,. (B.23) Here the second inequality uses \\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\leq\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}=\\|f\\|^{2} . Finally, ( B.19 ), ( B.23 ), and \\omega\\leq\\gamma_{\\rm gap} imply \\displaystyle\\bigl|\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)-\\|f\\|^{2}\\bigr| \\displaystyle=\\omega\\,|\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})|\\leq\\frac{\\omega}{2\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\leq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,.\\qed (B.24)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p7.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 863006,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 864591,
      "raw_sha256": "b3808232dea486d69580fbaa96827f8b3d4dc00e232cc23e2df6000fdd81a5be",
      "lf_sha256": "b3808232dea486d69580fbaa96827f8b3d4dc00e232cc23e2df6000fdd81a5be",
      "source_text": "The operators \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} and \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}} commute, so \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1} is self-adjoint on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0} . Moreover,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex19",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 864592,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 866257,
      "raw_sha256": "7a53fcb24ce6d0d1dc3683cf4f34cb5fea9a2a717c193297896dc7842f8ebd96",
      "lf_sha256": "7a53fcb24ce6d0d1dc3683cf4f34cb5fea9a2a717c193297896dc7842f8ebd96",
      "source_text": "I+(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1})^{2}=I+\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\\,,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-864656-866240",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 864656,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 866240,
      "raw_sha256": "740f553f652d97409f98f3ef9ae2623250d759fcdf7fd9ec09b456e44c37398c",
      "lf_sha256": "740f553f652d97409f98f3ef9ae2623250d759fcdf7fd9ec09b456e44c37398c",
      "source_text": "I+(\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1})^{2}=I+\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\\,,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p7.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 866258,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 867262,
      "raw_sha256": "39e7a99f71ce49add74a121317ed4722e695613b320703a59ea8db0419dd0516",
      "lf_sha256": "39e7a99f71ce49add74a121317ed4722e695613b320703a59ea8db0419dd0516",
      "source_text": "where the last identity uses \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I . By ( B.20 ),"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-867360-870435",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 867360,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 870435,
      "raw_sha256": "b6cc684a18e07c9f09d509464b1600cb86790be0c69064ee409732e3fe2198d8",
      "lf_sha256": "b6cc684a18e07c9f09d509464b1600cb86790be0c69064ee409732e3fe2198d8",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle 2\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}}) \\displaystyle=\\Bigl\\langle\\begin{pmatrix}f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\end{pmatrix}\\,,\\begin{pmatrix}I&-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\\\ -\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&-I\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\\\ f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\end{pmatrix}\\Bigr\\rangle\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p7.3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 870453,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 870591,
      "raw_sha256": "2c40525743e7f57b946d3bd69715239c55435bdaec4dbfcb198a13375e2bf6d8",
      "lf_sha256": "2c40525743e7f57b946d3bd69715239c55435bdaec4dbfcb198a13375e2bf6d8",
      "source_text": "The square of the block operator in this display is"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex21",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 870592,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 872936,
      "raw_sha256": "df83d337faca01e7b7525e584d9490b612b08c084eefbf554f58dae5fd6e7e81",
      "lf_sha256": "df83d337faca01e7b7525e584d9490b612b08c084eefbf554f58dae5fd6e7e81",
      "source_text": "\\begin{pmatrix}I&-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\\\ -\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&-I\\end{pmatrix}^{\\!2}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}&0\\\\ 0&\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-870656-872919",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 870656,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 872919,
      "raw_sha256": "089cd690a6fbd1f9136953f7e8ef56ca2b9dc1ba679868467a59527da526dbfe",
      "lf_sha256": "089cd690a6fbd1f9136953f7e8ef56ca2b9dc1ba679868467a59527da526dbfe",
      "source_text": "\\begin{pmatrix}I&-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\\\ -\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&-I\\end{pmatrix}^{\\!2}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}&0\\\\ 0&\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\\end{pmatrix}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p7.4",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 872937,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 873564,
      "raw_sha256": "ed0c4f995eabd4de8a39ee37ebda44236199ff2b2b8af3b232c9419a2d0f1772",
      "lf_sha256": "ed0c4f995eabd4de8a39ee37ebda44236199ff2b2b8af3b232c9419a2d0f1772",
      "source_text": "Since the block operator is self-adjoint and \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq\\gamma_{\\rm gap}I ,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Ex22",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 873565,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 875776,
      "raw_sha256": "add0628d50310d7f336820ef6cafe7fe14a0fd38b7cbe92757b0c71cd7439344",
      "lf_sha256": "add0628d50310d7f336820ef6cafe7fe14a0fd38b7cbe92757b0c71cd7439344",
      "source_text": "\\Bigl\\|\\begin{pmatrix}I&-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\\\ -\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&-I\\end{pmatrix}\\Bigr\\|=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\|\\leq\\frac{1}{\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-873629-875759",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 873629,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 875759,
      "raw_sha256": "73f716aba60139696c0316725abbd17fceb58dcc27e03b7b657c9033da430206",
      "lf_sha256": "73f716aba60139696c0316725abbd17fceb58dcc27e03b7b657c9033da430206",
      "source_text": "\\Bigl\\|\\begin{pmatrix}I&-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\\\ -\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&-I\\end{pmatrix}\\Bigr\\|=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\|\\leq\\frac{1}{\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p7.5",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 875777,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 875935,
      "raw_sha256": "1e301fbbcc3b499a1eb5112b0f46e0d2c01fcecf168bb6f19735b162904549df",
      "lf_sha256": "1e301fbbcc3b499a1eb5112b0f46e0d2c01fcecf168bb6f19735b162904549df",
      "source_text": "Applying this operator norm bound to the preceding quadratic form gives"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E23",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 875936,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 878117,
      "raw_sha256": "914bd55e78c5abd4eca907b961a6f5a9f0e85bb28e866a3d69cb1feda2742710",
      "lf_sha256": "914bd55e78c5abd4eca907b961a6f5a9f0e85bb28e866a3d69cb1feda2742710",
      "source_text": "|\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})|\\leq\\frac{1}{2\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,\\bigl(\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\bigr)\\leq\\frac{1}{2\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,. (B.23)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-875999-878100",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 875999,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 878100,
      "raw_sha256": "651cb2735ab861a3d2a57728817edec82d1a91e096fc3523042d866664407abf",
      "lf_sha256": "651cb2735ab861a3d2a57728817edec82d1a91e096fc3523042d866664407abf",
      "source_text": "|\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})|\\leq\\frac{1}{2\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,\\bigl(\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\bigr)\\leq\\frac{1}{2\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,. (B.23)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p7.6",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 878118,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 880319,
      "raw_sha256": "6ff89f1015632fd4187aab0ddd326e0568e3b65f9db7ec5c8fb1f12acacf74d8",
      "lf_sha256": "6ff89f1015632fd4187aab0ddd326e0568e3b65f9db7ec5c8fb1f12acacf74d8",
      "source_text": "Here the second inequality uses \\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}\\leq\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}=\\|f\\|^{2} . Finally, ( B.19 ), ( B.23 ), and \\omega\\leq\\gamma_{\\rm gap} imply"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-880416-883171",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 880416,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 883171,
      "raw_sha256": "00a96c1d4d60524f7215eb6274d6c637e8093481e00633f06943141d5f9ad2be",
      "lf_sha256": "00a96c1d4d60524f7215eb6274d6c637e8093481e00633f06943141d5f9ad2be",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle\\bigl|\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)-\\|f\\|^{2}\\bigr| \\displaystyle=\\omega\\,|\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})|\\leq\\frac{\\omega}{2\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\leq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,.\\qed (B.24)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Thmtheorem4",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "source-statement",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 883203,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 888587,
      "raw_sha256": "96cd87e4f50954a8826ee565fb398010f187f724336f5b75ca05fea570c9bc04",
      "lf_sha256": "96cd87e4f50954a8826ee565fb398010f187f724336f5b75ca05fea570c9bc04",
      "source_text": "Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function) . There exist universal constants c_{\\rm hyp},c_{0},c>0 such that the following holds. Set \\Lambda_{\\rho}\\coloneqq\\log(1/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})+\\Bigl(\\frac{\\rho}{\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\Bigr)^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\omega\\coloneqq\\frac{c_{\\rm hyp}\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\,. (B.25) If \\beta\\eta\\leq c_{0} , then every f\\in L_{0}^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}) satisfies \\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(\\mathsf{K}f)\\leq\\Bigl(1-\\frac{c\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\Bigr)\\,\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\,. (B.26)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 883664,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 884224,
      "raw_sha256": "59853598cff482c50f5e1e653df1312c69dfa90219b22197a8b97d98b90b9e11",
      "lf_sha256": "59853598cff482c50f5e1e653df1312c69dfa90219b22197a8b97d98b90b9e11",
      "source_text": "There exist universal constants c_{\\rm hyp},c_{0},c>0 such that the following holds. Set"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E25",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 884225,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 885936,
      "raw_sha256": "c49a2fc55595229e037cc738b2f8bf600ddeed1bc76eda51bf87ac4814eb7306",
      "lf_sha256": "c49a2fc55595229e037cc738b2f8bf600ddeed1bc76eda51bf87ac4814eb7306",
      "source_text": "\\Lambda_{\\rho}\\coloneqq\\log(1/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})+\\Bigl(\\frac{\\rho}{\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\Bigr)^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\omega\\coloneqq\\frac{c_{\\rm hyp}\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\,. (B.25)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-884288-885919",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 884288,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 885919,
      "raw_sha256": "c159bb4186ab30cd293563c404891b8e5c4dcaf001e973711b7c69eb850a86fc",
      "lf_sha256": "c159bb4186ab30cd293563c404891b8e5c4dcaf001e973711b7c69eb850a86fc",
      "source_text": "\\Lambda_{\\rho}\\coloneqq\\log(1/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})+\\Bigl(\\frac{\\rho}{\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}\\Bigr)^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\omega\\coloneqq\\frac{c_{\\rm hyp}\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\,. (B.25)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 885937,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 886898,
      "raw_sha256": "dfaf870e6cc80ec41766dcd9455574538d9744769fa741ba9b3e4fda1990d971",
      "lf_sha256": "dfaf870e6cc80ec41766dcd9455574538d9744769fa741ba9b3e4fda1990d971",
      "source_text": "If \\beta\\eta\\leq c_{0} , then every f\\in L_{0}^{2}(\\pi_{\\eta}) satisfies"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.E26",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 886899,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 888573,
      "raw_sha256": "3bdc91c30fd042bd4b0fc0448d828a99176073c8437a6ad703a05e4570e0bdf2",
      "lf_sha256": "3bdc91c30fd042bd4b0fc0448d828a99176073c8437a6ad703a05e4570e0bdf2",
      "source_text": "\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(\\mathsf{K}f)\\leq\\Bigl(1-\\frac{c\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\Bigr)\\,\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\,. (B.26)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-886962-888556",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 886962,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 888556,
      "raw_sha256": "2e53f5f2867f889fc67a67cf570cb4b7a86ef104a92b329f4fd85aec76c406bb",
      "lf_sha256": "2e53f5f2867f889fc67a67cf570cb4b7a86ef104a92b329f4fd85aec76c406bb",
      "source_text": "\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(\\mathsf{K}f)\\leq\\Bigl(1-\\frac{c\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\Bigr)\\,\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\,. (B.26)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.3",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "proof-container",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Modified L2 hypocoercivity and main theorem proof downstream of C.4; excluded from this bounded marginal PI delta.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 888588,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 970151,
      "raw_sha256": "627ba715434e7e1aa5afad7efa79265c359f9c12b735c8a5f96fd7aba66dfab3",
      "lf_sha256": "627ba715434e7e1aa5afad7efa79265c359f9c12b735c8a5f96fd7aba66dfab3",
      "source_text": "Proof. Take c_{0}\\leq 1/16 . Then \\gamma_{\\rm gap}\\leq 2\\sqrt{\\alpha\\eta}\\leq 1/2 , and consequently \\Lambda_{\\rho}\\geq\\log 2 . We compare the actual update with the idealized operator analyzed above. Let g\\coloneqq\\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id}f , g_{\\mathsf{P}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{P}g , and g_{\\mathsf{V}}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}g . By the definitions of \\mathsf{K} and \\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id} , \\displaystyle\\mathsf{K}f-\\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id}f \\displaystyle=\\mathsf{U}\\bigl[I+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\bigr]f_{\\perp} \\displaystyle=\\mathsf{U}\\bigl[\\rho f_{\\perp}+(1-\\rho)(I+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp})f_{\\perp}\\bigr]\\,. Using \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*} and \\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*} , the two components of this difference are \\displaystyle\\mathsf{P}(\\mathsf{K}f-\\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id}f) \\displaystyle=\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\bigl[I+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\bigr]f_{\\perp}\\,, \\displaystyle\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}(\\mathsf{K}f-\\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id}f) \\displaystyle=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\bigl[I+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\bigr]f_{\\perp}\\,. The same vector therefore determines both components of the error. Denote it by r_{\\rho}\\coloneqq\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\bigl[I+(1-\\rho)\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp}\\bigr]f_{\\perp}=\\rho f_{\\mathsf{V}}+(1-\\rho)r\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptr\\coloneqq\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp})f_{\\perp}\\,. Both r and r_{\\rho} belong to \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P},0} . In r_{\\rho} , the first term comes from refreshment, while the second measures the departure of the half turn from -I_{\\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp}} . Consequently, (\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{P}}=g_{\\mathsf{P}}+\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt(\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{V}}=g_{\\mathsf{V}}-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\,. (B.27) Substituting ( B.27 ) into the definition ( B.20 ) of the corrector \\mathscr{C} and expanding gives \\displaystyle\\mathscr{C}\\bigl((\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{P}},(\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{V}}\\bigr)-\\mathscr{C}(g_{\\mathsf{P}},g_{\\mathsf{V}}) \\displaystyle\\hskip 20.00003pt=\\bigl\\langle g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle+\\bigl\\langle g_{\\mathsf{V}},\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl(\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2}-\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2}\\bigr) \\displaystyle\\hskip 20.00003pt\\hskip 20.00003pt+{}\\bigl\\langle\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle-\\bigl\\langle\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho},g_{\\mathsf{V}}\\bigr\\rangle+\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2} \\displaystyle\\hskip 20.00003pt=\\bigl\\langle g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle+\\bigl\\langle\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl(\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2}+\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2}\\bigr)\\,. In the last equality, the two terms containing g_{\\mathsf{V}} cancel. For the terms linear in g_{\\mathsf{P}} , the commutation of \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} with \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}} and the identity \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I give \\displaystyle\\bigl\\langle g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle+\\bigl\\langle\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle \\displaystyle\\hskip 20.00003pt=\\bigl\\langle g_{\\mathsf{P}},(\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}+\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2})r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle=\\bigl\\langle g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle\\,. The same identity reduces the quadratic terms to \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\bigl(\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2}+\\|\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2}\\bigr)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|r_{\\rho}\\|^{2}\\,. Consequently, combined with ( B.21 ), \\displaystyle\\mathscr{C}\\bigl((\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{P}},(\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{V}}\\bigr)-\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}}) \\displaystyle\\hskip 10.00002pt=\\bigl[\\mathscr{C}\\bigl((\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{P}},(\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{V}}\\bigr)-\\mathscr{C}(g_{\\mathsf{P}},g_{\\mathsf{V}})\\bigr]+\\bigl[\\mathscr{C}(g_{\\mathsf{P}},g_{\\mathsf{V}})-\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})\\bigr] \\displaystyle\\hskip 10.00002pt=-\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}+\\bigl\\langle g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|r_{\\rho}\\|^{2}\\,. (B.28) Thus, it remains to estimate r_{\\rho} . Let \\mathsf{L}\\coloneqq(I+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp})\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}\\,. Since r=\\mathsf{L}^{*}f_{\\perp} , applying ( B.17 ) to \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v and then taking adjoints gives \\displaystyle\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\\|^{2}=\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp})f_{\\perp}\\|^{2} \\displaystyle\\leq C\\log(1/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\,. (B.29) Together with \\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}\\succeq\\gamma_{\\rm gap}I and \\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|\\leq\\|f_{\\perp}\\| , this gives \\displaystyle\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2} \\displaystyle\\leq 2\\rho^{2}\\,\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}+2(1-\\rho)^{2}\\,\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\\|^{2}\\leq C\\Lambda_{\\rho}\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\,. (B.30) Moreover, since \\mathsf{V}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*} and \\mathsf{H}_{\\perp\\perp} are contractions, \\|r_{\\rho}\\|\\leq\\rho\\,\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|+(1-\\rho)\\,\\|r\\|\\leq 2\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\| . The rotation formula for \\mathsf{K}_{\\rm id} gives \\|g_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}\\leq\\|g_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|g_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}=\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2} . Hence, Young’s inequality and ( B.30 ) give \\displaystyle\\bigl|\\bigl\\langle g_{\\mathsf{P}},\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\\rho}\\bigr\\rangle\\bigr| \\displaystyle\\leq\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\|g_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+C\\,\\|\\mathsf{\\Gamma}_{\\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\\rho}\\|^{2} \\displaystyle\\leq\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|^{2}+C\\Lambda_{\\rho}\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\,. Inserting these estimates into ( B.28 ), and using \\|f_{\\mathsf{V}}\\|\\leq\\|f_{\\perp}\\| and \\Lambda_{\\rho}\\geq\\log 2 , gives \\displaystyle\\mathscr{C}\\bigl((\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{P}},(\\mathsf{K}f)_{\\mathsf{V}}\\bigr)-\\mathscr{C}(f_{\\mathsf{P}},f_{\\mathsf{V}})\\leq-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+C\\Lambda_{\\rho}\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\,. (B.31) Finally, ( B.18 ) and ( B.31 ) give \\displaystyle\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(\\mathsf{K}f)-\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f) \\displaystyle\\leq-\\rho\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}+\\frac{c_{\\rm hyp}\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\,\\Bigl(-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+C\\Lambda_{\\rho}\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\Bigr) \\displaystyle=-\\frac{c_{\\rm hyp}\\rho}{2\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\,\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}-(1-Cc_{\\rm hyp})\\,\\rho\\,\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\,. Choose c_{\\rm hyp}\\leq 1 sufficiently small so that Cc_{\\rm hyp}\\leq 1/2 . Since \\Lambda_{\\rho}\\geq\\log 2 , the last display is then bounded above by -\\frac{c\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\,\\bigl(\\|f_{\\mathsf{P}}\\|^{2}+\\|f_{\\perp}\\|^{2}\\bigr)=-\\frac{c\\rho}{\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\,\\|f\\|^{2}\\,. It remains to compare the last norm with the Lyapunov function. The elementary inequality x/(a+x^{2})\\leq 1/(2\\sqrt{a}) , for a>0 and x\\geq 0 , gives \\frac{\\omega}{\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}=c_{\\rm hyp}\\,\\frac{\\rho/\\gamma_{\\rm gap}}{\\log(1/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})+(\\rho/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})^{2}}\\leq\\frac{c_{\\rm hyp}}{2\\sqrt{\\log(1/\\gamma_{\\rm gap})}}\\leq\\frac{c_{\\rm hyp}}{2\\sqrt{\\log 2}}\\leq 1\\,. Thus \\omega\\leq\\gamma_{\\rm gap} , and the upper bound in Lemma B.3 gives \\|f\\|^{2}\\geq\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\,. Consequently, \\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(\\mathsf{K}f)\\leq\\Bigl(1-\\frac{2c\\rho}{3\\Lambda_{\\rho}}\\Bigr)\\,\\mathscr{L}_{\\omega}(f)\\,, which is ( B.26 ) after renaming the universal constant. ∎"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A2.SS3.p8.1",
      "anchor_container": "A2.SS3",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
