      "lf_sha256": "0fce10f7786c9b57bbffc708cb6a90560955472c91fae09ce198d66c1afa1e04",
      "source_text": "\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}\\ell_{a,y}=\\ell_{a,y}\\cos t+a^{\\top}p\\sin t+\\int_{0}^{t}\\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\\widetilde{w}}\\sin(t-s)\\,\\mathrm{d}s"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Conditional affine half-turn estimates; independent downstream analytic lane, excluded from marginal PI construction.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 1142071,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1142869,
      "raw_sha256": "c3229eea958ba030f46fab80658a2dc78b5340fa9f000840163e908efc9730d3",
      "lf_sha256": "c3229eea958ba030f46fab80658a2dc78b5340fa9f000840163e908efc9730d3",
      "source_text": "in L^{2}(q_{y}\\otimes\\mathcal{N}(0,I)) . In particular,"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A3.E12",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Conditional affine half-turn estimates; independent downstream analytic lane, excluded from marginal PI construction.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 1142870,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1144808,
      "raw_sha256": "bd721dbcb7bcc1702531164275c1af9a44e9ddc3f75c348183d8bf36315d105f",
      "lf_sha256": "bd721dbcb7bcc1702531164275c1af9a44e9ddc3f75c348183d8bf36315d105f",
      "source_text": "(I+\\mathsf{T}_{\\pi}^{y,\\widetilde{w}})\\ell_{a,y}=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\\widetilde{w}}\\sin s\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\,. (C.12)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-1142933-1144791",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Conditional affine half-turn estimates; independent downstream analytic lane, excluded from marginal PI construction.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 1142933,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1144791,
      "raw_sha256": "1f6dabca2fcd20c1b1d7db63e03fea6329ec75dfb0e08b38e320df65d617286d",
      "lf_sha256": "1f6dabca2fcd20c1b1d7db63e03fea6329ec75dfb0e08b38e320df65d617286d",
      "source_text": "(I+\\mathsf{T}_{\\pi}^{y,\\widetilde{w}})\\ell_{a,y}=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\\widetilde{w}}\\sin s\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\,. (C.12)"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A3.SS2.2",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "proof-container",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Conditional affine half-turn estimates; independent downstream analytic lane, excluded from marginal PI construction.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 1144823,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1173466,
      "raw_sha256": "4dcf5723c98cf2087ac08fcca03b10f40639433f59399a6885ae2d59dbebc9e4",
      "lf_sha256": "4dcf5723c98cf2087ac08fcca03b10f40639433f59399a6885ae2d59dbebc9e4",
      "source_text": "Proof. The generator maps the position observable \\ell_{a,y} to the momentum observable a^{\\top}p , and maps a^{\\top}p back to -\\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\\widetilde{w}} . Thus, this pair evolves as a harmonic system with the additional term k_{a,\\widetilde{w}} , and variation of constants gives the claimed formula. We first establish the required L^{2} bounds and justify these generator identities for the unbounded observables. First, k_{a,\\widetilde{w}} is square integrable. Its first term is constant in (w,p) , while the absolute value of its second term is at most \\displaystyle 2\\,[p^{\\top}\\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\\widetilde{w})\\}]_{+}^{2}\\,\\frac{|a^{\\top}\\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\\widetilde{w})\\}|}{\\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\\widetilde{w})\\|^{2}} \\displaystyle\\leq 2\\,\\|a\\|\\,\\|p\\|^{2}\\,\\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\\widetilde{w})\\| \\displaystyle\\leq 2\\beta\\eta\\,\\|a\\|\\,\\|p\\|^{2}\\,\\|w-\\widetilde{w}\\|\\,. Since q_{y} is 1 -strongly log-concave and the momentum is Gaussian, this bound shows that k_{a,\\widetilde{w}} belongs to L^{2}(q_{y}\\otimes\\mathcal{N}(0,I)) . The same moment bounds give \\ell_{a,y},a^{\\top}p\\in L^{2}(q_{y}\\otimes\\mathcal{N}(0,I)) . Using a^{\\top}(R_{h}p-p)=-2(p^{\\top}h)(a^{\\top}h)/\\|h\\|^{2} and [u]_{+}u=[u]_{+}^{2} , the generator formula gives \\displaystyle\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{w}}\\ell_{a,y} \\displaystyle=a^{\\top}p\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{w}}(a^{\\top}p)=-\\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\\widetilde{w}}\\,. To justify these identities for the unbounded observables, set H_{\\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\\coloneqq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\{\\|w+g_{y}(\\widetilde{w})\\|^{2}+\\|p\\|^{2}\\} , which is preserved by both the flow and the bounces. Let \\chi_{R} be a smooth cutoff equal to one on [0,R] and zero on [2R,\\infty) . Conservation of H_{\\widetilde{w}} gives, for F\\in\\{\\ell_{a,y},a^{\\top}p\\} , \\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{w}}\\{\\chi_{R}(H_{\\widetilde{w}})F\\}=\\chi_{R}(H_{\\widetilde{w}})\\,\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{w}}F . Applying Dynkin’s formula and then letting R\\to\\infty in L^{2} , using the preceding integrability bounds and semigroup contractivity, yields \\displaystyle\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}\\ell_{a,y}-\\ell_{a,y} \\displaystyle=\\int_{0}^{t}\\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}(a^{\\top}p)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\,, \\displaystyle\\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}(a^{\\top}p)-a^{\\top}p \\displaystyle=\\int_{0}^{t}\\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}(-\\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\\widetilde{w}})\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\,. Applying variation of constants to this integral system gives \\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}\\ell_{a,y}=\\ell_{a,y}\\cos t+a^{\\top}p\\sin t+\\int_{0}^{t}\\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\\widetilde{w}}\\sin(t-s)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\\,. This is the first identity in the lemma. At t=\\pi , the homogeneous part is -\\ell_{a,y} and \\sin(\\pi-s)=\\sin s , which gives ( C.12 ). ∎"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A3.SS2.p9.1",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Conditional affine half-turn estimates; independent downstream analytic lane, excluded from marginal PI construction.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 1144975,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1147281,
      "raw_sha256": "82f879a0e647f244e56813025b65a25d24403800e99df0dcbd0bb19dd92d6180",
      "lf_sha256": "82f879a0e647f244e56813025b65a25d24403800e99df0dcbd0bb19dd92d6180",
      "source_text": "The generator maps the position observable \\ell_{a,y} to the momentum observable a^{\\top}p , and maps a^{\\top}p back to -\\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\\widetilde{w}} . Thus, this pair evolves as a harmonic system with the additional term k_{a,\\widetilde{w}} , and variation of constants gives the claimed formula. We first establish the required L^{2} bounds and justify these generator identities for the unbounded observables."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A3.SS2.p10.1",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
