      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1157593,
      "raw_sha256": "e6a4babbe182e80ad76761c1d2c9a2549b3feeba73b43061580aef79c3333085",
      "lf_sha256": "e6a4babbe182e80ad76761c1d2c9a2549b3feeba73b43061580aef79c3333085",
      "source_text": "Using a^{\\top}(R_{h}p-p)=-2(p^{\\top}h)(a^{\\top}h)/\\|h\\|^{2} and [u]_{+}u=[u]_{+}^{2} , the generator formula gives"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-1157691-1159767",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Conditional affine half-turn estimates; independent downstream analytic lane, excluded from marginal PI construction.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 1157691,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1159767,
      "raw_sha256": "806ad503d6a982c76494c0aba12ed99bf07ff8a110ef61e64e2f1528bff172e5",
      "lf_sha256": "806ad503d6a982c76494c0aba12ed99bf07ff8a110ef61e64e2f1528bff172e5",
      "source_text": "\\displaystyle\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{w}}\\ell_{a,y} \\displaystyle=a^{\\top}p\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{w}}(a^{\\top}p)=-\\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\\widetilde{w}}\\,."
    },
    {
      "region_id": "A3.SS2.p11.2",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "substantive-paragraph",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
      "reason": "Conditional affine half-turn estimates; independent downstream analytic lane, excluded from marginal PI construction.",
      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 1159785,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1165183,
      "raw_sha256": "540efc993c48af72af4073600266fb3651ea3ae4b27b6fbcfe70aefe626d0012",
      "lf_sha256": "540efc993c48af72af4073600266fb3651ea3ae4b27b6fbcfe70aefe626d0012",
      "source_text": "To justify these identities for the unbounded observables, set H_{\\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\\coloneqq\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\{\\|w+g_{y}(\\widetilde{w})\\|^{2}+\\|p\\|^{2}\\} , which is preserved by both the flow and the bounces. Let \\chi_{R} be a smooth cutoff equal to one on [0,R] and zero on [2R,\\infty) . Conservation of H_{\\widetilde{w}} gives, for F\\in\\{\\ell_{a,y},a^{\\top}p\\} , \\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{w}}\\{\\chi_{R}(H_{\\widetilde{w}})F\\}=\\chi_{R}(H_{\\widetilde{w}})\\,\\mathsf{L}_{y,\\widetilde{w}}F . Applying Dynkin’s formula and then letting R\\to\\infty in L^{2} , using the preceding integrability bounds and semigroup contractivity, yields"
    },
    {
      "region_id": "byte-1165281-1167228",
      "anchor_container": "A3.SS2",
      "kind": "display-equation",
      "disposition": "EXCLUDED",
