      "primary_start_utf8_byte": 1381673,
      "primary_end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 1384310,
      "raw_sha256": "26b66b1d7602972b433f1ffbe4b225c1905d789bfd9ed08910720c77bcdd13de",
      "lf_sha256": "26b66b1d7602972b433f1ffbe4b225c1905d789bfd9ed08910720c77bcdd13de",
      "source_text": "Proof. The upper bound is the Brascamp–Lieb inequality [ 3 , Chapter 4] applied to linear functions. The lower bound follows from the Cramér–Rao inequality for the location family generated by \\nu : \\displaystyle\\mathrm{Cov}_{\\nu}(Z) \\displaystyle\\succeq\\bigl(\\mathbb{E}_{\\nu}\\nabla^{2}W(Z)\\bigr)^{-1}\\succeq L^{-1}I\\,.\\qed",
